// TEST: An Int64 arrow read beside a Float64 argument is refused, never truncated (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3001 @ 8:19
// ============================================================================
// `c(0) + x` makes the read and `x` one type variable (functions/261), and the
// Int64 array decides it first: the Float64 `2.5` would have to narrow into
// it, which a call never does. It used to compile `x` as a defaulted Float64
// beside an Int64 read typed as the result -- a truncation g++ refused.
function g(c, x) = c(0) + x
let r = g([1, 2], 2.5)
